{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "ecd601db-360f-47b5-b920-5a089dc9424a",
    "name": "P0Puti.uz API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Tests for the P0Puti.uz backend. Full API reference: `server/openapi.yml`.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Import this collection and `p0puti-local.postman_environment.json`, then select the **P0Puti – local** environment.\n2. In the environment, set **botToken** to the `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` from `server/.env`. The login requests use it to sign a test Telegram login, so you don't need the mini app.\n3. Optional: set **userA_telegramId** to your own Telegram ID to receive the bot's messages. User B is a made-up ID, so its bot messages fail in the bot log; that's expected.\n4. Start the API and the worker (`node dist/main.js`, `node dist/worker.main.js`). The bot is optional.\n5. Run the whole collection with the Collection Runner, top to bottom. Later requests use IDs saved by earlier ones.\n\n**Safety:** the bot token can sign a login for any Telegram user. Keep it only in your local environment's current value, and never put your production token in a shared Postman workspace.\n\n**Expected failure:** \"User A cannot post an ad with user B's vehicle\" fails until the vehicle ownership check is merged."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "description": "Logs in two test users. Run this first: everything else needs their tokens.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": []
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as user A",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/telegram",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "telegram"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"initData\": \"{{initData}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Signs a Telegram login exactly like Telegram does, using the bot token from the environment,",
                  "// so you can log in without opening the mini app. Never use your production bot token here.",
                  "const CryptoJS = require('crypto-js');",
                  "const botToken = pm.environment.get('botToken');",
                  "if (!botToken) {",
                  "  throw new Error('Set botToken in the environment: the TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from server/.env');",
                  "}",
                  "const user = {",
                  "  id: Number(pm.environment.get('userA_telegramId') || 700000001),",
                  "  first_name: 'Test',",
                  "  last_name: 'User A',",
                  "  username: 'p0puti_test_a',",
                  "};",
                  "const fields = { auth_date: String(Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)), user: JSON.stringify(user) };",
                  "const dataCheckString = Object.keys(fields).sort().map((k) => k + '=' + fields[k]).join('\\n');",
                  "const secretKey = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(botToken, 'WebAppData');",
                  "const hash = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(dataCheckString, secretKey).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
                  "pm.variables.set('initData', Object.entries({ ...fields, hash })",
                  "  .map(([k, v]) => k + '=' + encodeURIComponent(v))",
                  "  .join('&'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Login succeeds (201)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains an access token', () => pm.expect(body.user.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.user.data.accessToken);",
                  "pm.environment.set('userId', body.user.data.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login as user B (second test user)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
